---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE_NAME } from '../config';
---
<PageLayout
  title="Terms of Use – Fair, Simple Rules | HugMyFile"
  description="The rules for using HugMyFile: only process files you own or have rights to, use only your own signature, and tools are provided as is."
  path="/terms"
  h1="Terms of Use"
  lead="Plain-language rules for using the site."
  updated="October 29, 2026"
>
  <p>By using {SITE_NAME} you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the site.</p>

  <h2>1. What the site does</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE_NAME} offers free tools that process files directly in your web browser. Files are not uploaded to us. You are
    responsible for keeping your own copies of your files and for downloading any results you want to keep.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Use only files you have the right to use</h2>
  <p>
    You may only process files that you own or that you have permission to use and change. Do not use the tools to infringe
    anyone’s copyright, privacy or other rights, to remove protections, or for anything illegal.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Signatures</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Only create and use your own signature. Using someone else’s signature is illegal.</strong> The signature tools add a
    picture of a signature to a file. This is a visual signature, not a certified digital signature, and it may not be accepted
    for every purpose. Check what your recipient requires.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Passport, visa and ID photos</h2>
  <p>
    The photo maker helps you crop and size a picture. {SITE_NAME} is not affiliated with any government. Always check the
    official photo requirements for your application; we cannot guarantee that a photo will be accepted.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Provided “as is”</h2>
  <p>
    The tools are provided “as is” and “as available”, without warranties of any kind, express or implied, including fitness for
    a particular purpose and accuracy of results (for example text recognition). To the fullest extent permitted by law,
    {SITE_NAME} is not liable for any loss or damage arising from your use of the site, including lost or corrupted files.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Audience</h2>
  <p>The site is intended for a general audience and is not directed at children under 13.</p>

  <h2>7. Trademarks</h2>
  <p>
    Product names such as WhatsApp, iPhone, Safari or Chrome are mentioned only to describe compatibility. All trademarks belong to
    their respective owners. {SITE_NAME} is not affiliated with them.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Open-source software</h2>
  <p>The tools are built with open-source software, listed with their licenses on our <a href="/licenses">Open-source credits</a> page.</p>

  <h2>9. Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update these terms from time to time. The “Last updated” date shows when they last changed.</p>
</PageLayout>
